
# LEGO Train Switch Controller

Software for controlling a LEGO train track switch
using a Seeed Studio XIAO ESP32-S3 and a DMS-MG90 servo.

## Hardware

- Seeed Studio XIAO ESP32-S3
- DMS-MG90 positional servo
- External regulated 5V power supply (servo works on 4.8-6V)
- LEGO plastic train track switch

## Software

- PlatformIO
- Arduino framework
- ESP32Servo library

## Wiring

| Servo wire | Connection |
|---|---|
| Brown | External power GND |
| Red | External 5V |
| Orange | XIAO D0 |

**Important:** XIAO GND and external power GND must be connected together.

## Controls

The current test program accepts commands through the Serial Monitor.

| Command | Action |
|---|---|
| L / l | Move to left position |
| R / r | Move to right position |

## Servo positions

Current test values:

- Left: 75 degrees
- Right: 115 degrees

These calibrated to the original LEGO switch.

## Status

## Status

- Working with the original LEGO plastic track switch.
- Not yet tested with 3D-printed switch mechanisms.
- 3D-printed mechanisms are expected to require less force, but compatibility and movement still need proper testing.
